//
// Firefly.xcconfig — committed. Nothing in here signs anything on its
// own; CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED = NO in project.yml still wins for the
// committed project, so a clean checkout keeps building with no team
// and no certificate (A01_AC1).
//
// The #include? below is OPTIONAL (the "?" — .xcconfig's own syntax for
// "include this file if it exists, say nothing if it doesn't"). It pulls
// in Local.xcconfig, a git-ignored, per-developer file that is not
// committed and cannot be, because it holds a personal DEVELOPMENT_TEAM.
// Copy Local.xcconfig.example to Local.xcconfig, fill in your team id,
// and flip CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED back to YES yourself to run on a device
// (see app/README.md, "Run on the iPhone"). Nobody's team id ever
// reaches this repo's history.
//
#include? "Local.xcconfig"
